description=Small fixes and finishing touches for vanilla. Cold packs and coolers work: chill a cold pack in a fridge (half way) or a freezer (fully), or leave it out below freezing, then put it in a cooler. The cooler keeps food as cold as a fridge does, about 6 hours for each frozen pack (a sandbox setting), and the packs and the cooler show how cold they are in their names. A Collection button on the sidebar opens a checklist for each character of the skill books, recipe magazines, VHS tapes, CDs, key rings, mementos and tools they own: tick what you have, and those items say so in their tooltip and are set Unwanted, so they grey out and Take All leaves them. Cigarette packs on gas station, convenience store, liquor store and tobacconist shelves come full, not half-smoked. Item tooltips say more: the read time left on skill books (and on novels with Vitality's reading), uses left on drainables (charge for batteries), weapon numbers that open up as you level the weapon's skill, and for clothing the body parts it covers and how it compares with what you wear (its own sandbox page). Also, when Item Rarity UI is active, modded items get a rarity colour worked out from the loot lists the same way Item Rarity UI does it for vanilla. Singleplayer only for now.
